  "id": "gene-imprinting",
  "term": "gene imprinting",
  "definition": "Gene imprinting is a parent-of-origin effect in which a gene’s biological impact depends on whether it was inherited from the father or the mother. In this packet, it is used to explain why paternally inherited variants can be linked to disease risk while the same variants inherited maternally may not be.",
